{
  "requirement": "`ValidationCache::new()` creates an empty cache for running criteria without\nan agent.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<D: Domain> ValidationCache<D> {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two obligations. `ValidationCache::new()` must return an empty cache, and the cache must be usable for running criteria without an agent.\n\n- **Unit test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent]` calls `new()` and asserts three things. `agent` is `None`, `sources` is `None`, and the `outlines` map is empty. These cover the \"no agent\" half and the emptiness of the file-related state.\n- **Integration test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path]` builds a cache with `ValidationCache::<Application>::new()`. It then uses that cache with no agent to load outlines: a missing file errors first, and a later load succeeds. This shows that a fresh cache works without an agent.\n- **Unasserted fields:** The tests don't assert on the private `nodes` map or on `source_addresses`. `new()` is `Self::default()` (`crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#impl[ValidationCache<D>]/fn[new]`). The `Default` impl (`crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#impl[ValidationCache<D>/Default]`) initializes those two maps with `Default::default()`, with no conditional logic. I judged leaving them unasserted acceptable.\n\nI found no gap.",
